    "text": "A plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is parallel to two lines whose direction ratios are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and it contains the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> intersect the co-ordinate axes at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></math> making the intercepts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is the volume of the tetrahedron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is the origin and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math>, then the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to",
